    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Code-page-as-webresource-pane" location="src/solutions/CalendarSidePane/">Mirror the Vite singlefile + main.tsx bootstrap + webresource-pane hosting; adapt for the Navigator 3-tab scaffold.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Theme detection + scale" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkModal/scaledTheme.ts">Detect light/dark (prefers-color-scheme + theme URL param) and apply the scaled Fluent theme + useUiScale for NFR-07.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Register against the host" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SidePane/SprkSidePaneHost.tsx">Render the Navigator body via a sidePaneRegistry entry ({ id, icon, title, order, component }); one entry = one rail icon.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor (FULL) + model-tier (sonnet) + effort (high) per task-execute Step 0.5; load the knowledge files and read the CalendarSidePane/EventDetailSidePane reference solutions.</step>
    <step order="1">Scaffold src/solutions/NavigatorPane/ (package.json, vite.config.ts singlefile, main.tsx) mirroring CalendarSidePane; wire npm install --legacy-peer-deps.</step>
    <step order="2">Build NavigatorBody.tsx as a shared component: 3-tab layout (Recent / Pinned / Views) + a persistent top-of-pane search-bar placeholder; tabs are scaffold only (no data wiring this task).</step>
    <step order="3">Add theme detection (prefers-color-scheme + theme URL param) and apply scaledTheme + useUiScale so --sprk-ui-scale is respected; wrap portalled surfaces in their own FluentProvider (ADR-021).</step>
    <step order="4">Register the Navigator body against SprkSidePaneHost via a sidePaneRegistry entry so it mounts as a webresource pane driving one rail icon.</step>
    <step order="5">Handle the no-Xrm case: when getXrm() returns undefined (non-MDA surface), render a safe empty state and do not throw.</step>
    <step order="6">Author __tests__/NavigatorBody.test.tsx: tab scaffold + search-bar placeholder render; light AND dark render correctly; portal FluentProvider re-wrap present (ADR-021); --sprk-ui-scale applies; no-Xrm empty state does not throw.</step>
    <step order="7">Cache-clear + recompile @spaarke/ui-components, then Vite npm run build; confirm the bundle builds singlefile and a known string is present in the built HTML.</step>
    <step order="8">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set task 040 status to completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/spaarke-side-pane-navigation-history-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the current UCI build does not host the code page reliably as a pageType:'webresource' pane (mount/theme/scale failing), STOP and escalate (root §6.5 — ties to the FR-00 spike / Path A fallback) rather than forcing a form-handler or BFF workaround that violates the project MUST-NOT rules.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>src/solutions/CalendarSidePane/ and src/solutions/EventDetailSidePane/ — shipping Vite code pages hosted as webresource panes (chrome + theme + mount pattern).</existing>
    <extension>Pattern-reuse but not extension: those are distinct EventDetail/Calendar surfaces with their own bodies; NavigatorPane is a separate surface (3-tab Recent/Pinned/Views quick-access) with its own registry entry and body. Mirror their code-page mechanics, do not extend their components.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the NavigatorPane surface there is no docked Navigator shell for the tabs, capture, and search to render into — the core user need (one-gesture cross-device quick-access, spec §1) fails and tasks 041/042/050/051/052/060/070 have nowhere to build.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Tab scaffold + search bar render in light and dark">
      <steps>
        <step>Mount NavigatorBody in light theme; confirm Recent/Pinned/Views tabs + search-bar placeholder.</step>
        <step>Re-mount in dark theme (data-theme=dark / prefers-color-scheme dark).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All three tabs + the persistent search bar render with Fluent v9 tokens honoring light and dark correctly (no hardcoded colors).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="--sprk-ui-scale applies (ADR-021 portal check)">
      <steps>
        <step>Mount with a non-default --sprk-ui-scale value and inspect the applied scaled Fluent theme.</step>
        <step>Inspect any portalled surface for a FluentProvider re-wrap.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The scaled theme reflects --sprk-ui-scale; portalled content is wrapped in its own FluentProvider (ADR-021 portal gotcha).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="No-Xrm surface degrades gracefully">
      <steps>
        <step>Mount the body where getXrm() returns undefined (non-MDA context).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>A safe empty state renders and the page does not throw.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Recompile @spaarke/ui-components; run Jest render tests; Vite npm run build (cache-clear first).</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/NavigatorPane/src/main.tsx</output>
