  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the NavigatorPane solution, when built with Vite singlefile, then it produces a singlefile bundle whose built HTML contains a verified known string.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the app pane, when the Navigator body registers against SprkSidePaneHost, then it mounts as a pageType:'webresource' pane driving exactly one rail icon.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the mounted body, when it renders, then the Recent/Pinned/Views tab scaffold and the persistent search-bar placeholder are visible.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given light and dark themes, when the body renders, then Fluent v9 tokens honor both correctly with a portal FluentProvider re-wrap (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a non-default --sprk-ui-scale, when the body renders, then the scaled Fluent theme respects it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given no Xrm on the surface, when the body mounts, then it renders a safe empty state and does not throw.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All render tests pass; Vite build green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Maps to spec FR-01 (surface) + FR-11 (search scaffold) and plan.md Phase 4 task 040. Tabs are scaffold only here; data wiring lands in 041/042 (Recent), 050/051/052 (Pinned), 060 (Views), 070 (search). Body is a shared component for phase-2 dashboard-widget reuse (NFR-08). Run /conflict-check before any @spaarke/ui-components PR.

COMPLETED 2026-08-13 (sonnet, FULL rigor). Escalation trigger did NOT fire. Built src/solutions/NavigatorPane/ (Vite singlefile code page mirroring EventDetailSidePane's simpler vite.config — no resolveSharedLibDeps plugin needed since only @spaarke/ui-components' pre-built dist/ is consumed): main.tsx renders SprkSidePaneHost (task 011) as the pane's root component and registers NavigatorBody as its sole sidePaneRegistry contributor at module-load time — this is how "one contributor = one rail icon" (spec FR-01/FR-13) is satisfied by a single webresource bundle. NavigatorBody.tsx = the 3-tab (Recent/Pinned/Views) + persistent search-bar-placeholder scaffold, authored as a standalone shared component (NFR-08): it resolves its OWN theme (resolveCodePageTheme + useUiScale/scaleTheme) rather than depending on a parent, explicitly re-wraps its one portalled surface (the search-bar info Tooltip) in its own FluentProvider (ADR-021 Option A), and renders a safe empty state when getXrm() is undefined.

Deviations (Path C — pivot to comply, CLAUDE.md §6.5): the task's constraint text says "theme detection (prefers-color-scheme + theme URL param)" — used the codebase's canonical `resolveCodePageTheme()`/`setupCodePageThemeListener()` (localStorage -> URL flags -> navbar DOM) instead of a raw OS `prefers-color-scheme` media query, because ADR-021 + xrmContext.ts + themeStorage.ts all explicitly state OS-level dark-mode detection is NOT consulted (Spaarke theme system controls all surfaces), and every sibling code page (CalendarSidePane, EventDetailSidePane) uses this exact utility. See notes/task-040-navigatorpane-deviations.md.

Self-run code-review (Step 9.5) found one real issue, fixed before completion: the search-bar info Tooltip trigger was a bare, non-focusable `Info16Regular` icon (WCAG 2.1 AA / ADR-021 MUST gap) with `Tooltip relationship="label"` — which would have silently overridden the icon's own aria-label with the (different) tooltip text. Fixed: trigger is now a `Button appearance="transparent"` (keyboard-focusable, matches the SprkSidePaneHost rail-icon precedent) and `relationship="description"` (adds aria-describedby without clobbering the explicit aria-label). Self-run adr-check: 0 violations against ADR-006/021/022.

Build (Vite npm run build, NOT build:prod; cache-cleared rm -rf dist/ node_modules/.vite/ .vite/ before every build; @spaarke/ui-components recompiled first via `npm run build` (tsc) in that package): green. Known-string verified in dist/index.html: `<title>Spaarke Navigator</title>` plus NavigatorBody-source strings ("Navigator is unavailable outside a Dataverse session", "Search wiring lands in a later task") all present post-cache-clear rebuild — proves a fresh bundle, not stale. `npx tsc --noEmit`: clean. `npx jest` (jest.config.cjs, ts-jest + jsdom): 5/5 passing — required adding `@testing-library/dom` (missing peer of `@testing-library/react`), extending `transformIgnorePatterns` to allow the shared lib's transitive ESM deps (d3-force/d3-dispatch/d3-quadtree/d3-timer/marked — mirrors Spaarke.UI.Components' own jest.config.js allow-list), and a `moduleNameMapper` react/react-dom dedupe (this `file:`-referenced package has its OWN un-hoisted node_modules/react, distinct from the consumer's — without forcing single-instance resolution, `useUiScale`'s hooks execute against a react module with no live dispatcher: "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'useState')"). No eslint config exists at this level (matches CalendarSidePane/EventDetailSidePane precedent — lint script present as boilerplate, not enforced per-package).</notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
